<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Privacy manifest for the phone app target (App).

  SCOPE: required-reason API declarations only. NSPrivacyTracking,
  NSPrivacyTrackingDomains and NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes are deliberately
  ABSENT rather than declared empty, because the data-flow evidence for this
  build is not yet complete. Omission is not a claim of "none"; see the
  handback report for the exact unresolved fields.

  SOURCE MAPPING (first-party code compiled into the App target):

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults -> 1C8F.1
      UserDefaults(suiteName: AppConstants.AppGroupID), shared with the app
      extensions via the App Group container:
        AppDelegate.swift:23
        Utilities/Utils.swift:50

    NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults -> CA92.1
      UserDefaults.standard, accessed only within this app's own container:
        AppDelegate.swift:345
        Utilities/Utils.swift:28,29  (reset-on-uninstall housekeeping)

    The six embedded app extensions (Share, Widgets, PushProvider,
    NotificationContent, Intents, NotificationService) contain no first-party
    required-reason API use in their own sources; they link the dynamic
    Shared.framework, which carries its own manifest. They therefore do not
    receive a copy of this file. This is a SOURCE-LEVEL determination;
    per-binary symbol coverage has not been verified in this lane.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
